      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many political analysts in Eastern Europe and Russia argue that NATO's eastward expansion since the 1990s violated unspoken security assurances, creating deep skepticism about the alliance's neutrality in the region. Critics contend that this shift from a defensive umbrella to an aggressive political entity has eroded trust, leading to a permanent sense of encirclement and propaganda narratives that justified coercion or conflict. Consequently, this perceived threat has fueled a foundation of mistrust that makes regional de-escalation significantly more challenging today.",
